\ The canonical choice of year 5000 for a calculation day.
\ Enumerate pairs of gates that contain c and are at most 5778 days
\ apart. At least six gate intervals are required for a valid year.
\ Eligible pairs are sorted by duration and then earlier opening gate.
\ Ask bowl 1 with seal 10 using the sauce for (c,c).
\ The chosen candidate is year 5000, and no alternative may replace it.
\
\ Gate gaps are never guessed: every new gate comes from its own
\ full canonical sauce calculation, computed once during the scan.
\ The gate ledger and candidate ledger are released after selection.
\ The current day-axis adapter is still limited to native CAL numbers.
\ Compilation and execution with CAL are not yet verified.

A gate mark is a thing with
  a calendar day called position,
  a number called index.

A year option is a thing with
  a year candidate.

The nearby gate ledger is some gate marks.
The eligible year ledger is some year options.
The opening gate mark is a gate mark.
The closing gate mark is a gate mark.
The examined year option is a year option.
The selected year option is a year option.
The chosen year is a year candidate.
The working year candidate is a year candidate.
The year selection day is a calendar day.
The lower gate cutoff is a calendar day.
The upper gate cutoff is a calendar day.
The eligible year count is a number.
The selected year rank is a number.
The year selection success is a number.
The selected year available is a number.

\ Copy the current gate-walk position into a new linked mark.
To create a gate mark:
  Allocate memory for the gate mark.
  Put the gate walk's current position into the gate mark's position.
  Put the gate walk's current index into the gate mark's index.

\ The positive scan appends marks in ascending chronological order.
To record positive gate marks:
  Create a gate mark.
  Append the gate mark to the nearby gate ledger.

\ The negative scan prepends marks in ascending chronological order.
To record negative gate marks:
  Create a gate mark.
  Prepend the gate mark to the nearby gate ledger.

\ Scan positive gates only if the requested window reaches Foundation.
To gather the positive gate marks:
  If the upper gate cutoff is less than -15055671, exit.
  Put 0 into the gate walk's current index.
  Put -15055671 into the gate walk's current position.
  Loop.
    Move to the next positive gate.
    If the gate step budget's exhausted is 1, exit.
    If the gate walk's current position is greater than the upper gate cutoff, break.
    If the gate walk's current position is less than the lower gate cutoff, repeat.
    Record positive gate marks.
  Repeat.

\ Scan negative gates only if the requested window reaches Foundation.
To gather the negative gate marks:
  If the lower gate cutoff is greater than -15055671, exit.
  Put 0 into the gate walk's current index.
  Put -15055671 into the gate walk's current position.
  Loop.
    Move to the next negative gate.
    If the gate step budget's exhausted is 1, exit.
    If the gate walk's current position is less than the lower gate cutoff, break.
    If the gate walk's current position is greater than the upper gate cutoff, repeat.
    Record negative gate marks.
  Repeat.

\ The original day-zero gate is inserted only when it is in range.
To gather the nearby gate marks for a calendar day:
  Destroy the nearby gate ledger.
  Put the calendar day into the year selection day.
  Put the calendar day into the lower gate cutoff.
  Subtract 5778 from the lower gate cutoff.
  Put the calendar day into the upper gate cutoff.
  Add 5778 to the upper gate cutoff.
  If the lower gate cutoff is less than or equal to -15055671,
    record Foundation in the nearby gate ledger.
  Gather the negative gate marks.
  Gather the positive gate marks.

\ Create the Foundation gate without accidentally reading a previous
\ value left in the gate walk by some unrelated calculation.
To record Foundation in the nearby gate ledger:
  Put 0 into the gate walk's current index.
  Put -15055671 into the gate walk's current position.
  If the upper gate cutoff is less than -15055671, exit.
  Record positive gate marks.

\ Copy a gate pair to the candidate and derive both durations.
To measure gate pairs for candidate selection:
  Put the opening gate mark's position into the working year candidate's opening day.
  Put the closing gate mark's position into the working year candidate's closing day.
  Put the opening gate mark's index into the working year candidate's opening index.
  Put the closing gate mark's index into the working year candidate's closing index.
  Measure the working year candidate.

\ The first eligible year is placed before the next longer candidate.
\ Equal lengths are sorted by earlier opening gate.
To insert a sorted year candidate:
  Create a year option.
  Put the working year candidate into the year option's year candidate.
  Put the eligible year ledger's first into the examined year option.
  Loop.
    If the examined year option is nil, break.
    If the working year candidate comes before the examined year option's year candidate,
      insert the year option into the eligible year ledger before the examined year option; exit.
    Put the examined year option's next into the examined year option.
  Repeat.
  Append the year option to the eligible year ledger.

To create a year option:
  Allocate memory for the year option.

\ A single opening gate has only later closing candidates.
\ Because gates are sorted, a too-long pair ends this inner scan.
To gather candidate years for the opening gate:
  Put the opening gate mark's next into the closing gate mark.
  Loop.
    If the closing gate mark is nil, break.
    Measure gate pairs for candidate selection.
    If the working year candidate's year length is greater than 5778, break.
    If the working year candidate contains the year selection day,
      insert a sorted year candidate; add 1 to the eligible year count.
    Put the closing gate mark's next into the closing gate mark.
  Repeat.

\ Stop opening-gate enumeration as soon as open >= calculation day.
To gather eligible year candidates:
  Destroy the eligible year ledger.
  Put 0 into the eligible year count.
  Put the nearby gate ledger's first into the opening gate mark.
  Loop.
    If the opening gate mark is nil, break.
    If the opening gate mark's position is greater than or equal to the year selection day, break.
    Gather candidate years for the opening gate.
    Put the opening gate mark's next into the opening gate mark.
  Repeat.

\ Retrieve a one-based rank without ever dereferencing a missing
\ list entry. The chosen year is updated only after validation succeeds.
\ Failed rank requests leave the prior chosen year unchanged.
To read the selected year candidate:
  Put 0 into the selected year available.
  If the selected year rank is less than 1, exit.
  If the selected year rank is greater than the eligible year count, exit.
  Put the eligible year ledger's first into the selected year option.
  Put 1 into a current rank number.
  Loop.
    If the selected year option is nil, exit.
    If the current rank number is the selected year rank, break.
    Put the selected year option's next into the selected year option.
    Add 1 to the current rank number.
  Repeat.
  If the selected year option is nil, exit.
  Put the selected year option's year candidate into the chosen year.
  Put 1 into the selected year available.

\ The year-5000 choice uses the sauce for (c,c), not the last gate
\ pair or a cutlet year whose identity is already known.
To choose year five thousand for the calculation day:
  Put the year selection day into the example's calculation day.
  Put the year selection day into the example's requested day.
  Answer the example.
  Copy the example into the sauce input.
  Make the complete sauce.
  Put 1 into the seal inquiry's bowl identity.
  Put 10 into the seal inquiry's seal number.
  Begin a seal inquiry.
  Convert the eligible year count to a string.
  Put the string into a year option count wide quantity.
  Determine canonical equal selection given the year option count wide quantity.
  Convert the seal inquiry's selected quantity to the selected year rank.
  Read the selected year candidate.

\ This routine is the year-5000 entrypoint.
\ A zero result status is an explicit failure, never a fabricated year.
To find year five thousand for a calendar day:
  Put 0 into the year selection success.
  Begin bounded gate walking.
  Gather the nearby gate marks for the calendar day.
  If the gate step budget's exhausted is 1,
    destroy the nearby gate ledger; exit.
  Gather eligible year candidates.
  If the eligible year count is 0,
    destroy the eligible year ledger; destroy the nearby gate ledger; exit.
  Choose year five thousand for the calculation day.
  If the selected year available is not 1,
    destroy the eligible year ledger; destroy the nearby gate ledger; exit.
  Put 1 into the year selection success.
  Destroy the eligible year ledger.
  Destroy the nearby gate ledger.
